Randomly generated WOW's aren't really a problem.  I forget what we concluded
the odds were at the end of that long debate a while ago, but it was on the
order of 1/10000 per level.  Not really worth worrying about.  Once in a 
blue moon you may find one, get great equipement, get overconfident, and
die in some stupid death as usual.

I think the main purpose of the WOW in the castle (or under a boulder as it
used to be in some older version), was to allow you to pick up the few things
you really need before going to Hell.  For example, if you have teleport and 
not teleport control, the game is pretty frustrating.  Instead of searching
on and on for tengu's or rings, now is you chance to get it, and just go on
with the game. (or magic resistant armor, or whatever you still need).

The WOW will probably remain a fixture of the castle, as a big encouragement
for people to get that far.  Something to allow people to go on to bigger and
better things afterwards.  As has been pointed out numerous times, it's very
frustrating to invest all the time required to get a character to the castle,
and then have them die.  With the WOW there, you probably have no one but 
yourself to blame if you use all the wishes, and still die. 
